  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The short answer",
      "items": [
        "Admission explores the machine over its contract's whole declared domain: effect invariants over every path, state invariants in every state, liveness, stops, waits and batteries",
        "The certificate digests every file and local module and is signed",
        "a worker with a trust store refuses any machine whose files differ by a byte"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Not shown here",
      "items": [
        "The runtime host that steps the same machine, and the worker's refusal, which is question four's plugin",
        "Connected but out of scope: Sinks, Temporal server, SAM machine host, PolyflowPlugin, vet"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Doctrine",
      "items": [
        "Every check is a consistency check, not a proof — admission is exhaustive only over the finite domains a contract declares, and the guard decides only what its rules express",
        "The certificate is the version — the buildId is a digest of what was certified, and under Worker Versioning the worker runs under that build id or not at all"
      ]
    }
  ]
